This repository holds two different things under two different terms.

The source code, the tests and the tools are ours and are offered under the
MIT licence below.

The tables are not. Most of them are the files under src/data, and a handful
of smaller ones -- the code pages, the pair classes, the dictionary buckets --
are written out inside src/text.c. They are all read out of Berkeley Speech
Technologies' own binaries: the letter-to-sound rules, the dictionaries, the
phoneme and duration tables, the excitation and gain tables of the lattice, so
that the library can speak without those binaries being present. That data is
Berkeley Speech Technologies' work, and later HumanWare's. The MIT licence
below covers our code and says nothing about their tables, which we are in no
position to license to anyone. Use them where you have the right to.

